/*
 * zakpay.mjs
 *
 * Paying online moves inside the popup.
 *
 * Until now "Pay online" left the popup for Shopify's checkout, which asked
 * for an email, showed its own thank-you page, and never came back. Now,
 * with the shop's Razorpay keys entered on the app's settings page, the
 * popup opens Razorpay's checkout right where it is (UPI, card, net
 * banking), and the moment the money is confirmed the app writes the paid
 * order itself - the same way it writes a Cash on Delivery one - and shows
 * its own "Payment received - order confirmed" screen with the chime,
 * then goes on to the order page. No Shopify checkout, no email asked.
 *
 * How the money is kept safe:
 *   - the amount is worked out on the server from Shopify's own prices and
 *     the real discount codes; the page cannot change it
 *   - nothing is written to Shopify until Razorpay has confirmed the payment
 *     and its signature checks out
 *   - a phone that drops its connection right after paying is covered: the
 *     app's clock job asks Razorpay for paid orders every ten minutes and
 *     writes any order the browser never came back for
 *   - one payment can only ever become one order, even if the browser and
 *     the clock job arrive in the same second
 *
 * Without the keys, nothing changes: Pay online goes to Shopify's checkout
 * exactly as before.
 *
 * Two things the live logs caught are mended in the same run:
 *
 *   - A refund was never announced on WhatsApp. Shopify creates the refund
 *     with its transaction still "pending" - the bank has not taken it yet,
 *     which is why the email says three to five working days - and the app
 *     was waiting for settled money before saying anything. refunds/create
 *     fires once and never again, so that message was never sent at all.
 *     Order Z1014 on 8 September is the case: the customer had Shopify's
 *     refund email and nothing from us. Pending now counts; a refund with
 *     no transaction behind it (an order nobody ever paid for, cancelled to
 *     tidy the list) still says nothing, which is right.
 *
 *   - The second abandoned-cart reminder was reaching nobody. The template
 *     carries a "copy the code" button, and Meta throws the whole message
 *     away with 131008 unless the coupon travels in a component of its own.
 *     Every one of them failed. The sender now reads that button off the
 *     template and hands it the code.
 *
 * Every file it touches is copied to ..\zak-bak first, and a file that is
 * not the version this script was built against is left alone and named.
 * Run it from the repo root, after zakfix.mjs.
 */

import { readFileSync, writeFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, copyFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { join, dirname } from "node:path";
import { createHash } from "node:crypto";

